Title: First Duplicate Finder in Array

Main Goal: This code defines a function that finds the first duplicate element in an array. The obfuscated code, when decoded, implements a simple algorithm using a Set data structure to track seen elements. As it iterates through the input array, it checks if each element already exists in the Set. If found, it returns that duplicate element immediately. If no duplicates are found after checking all elements, it returns -1.

The obfuscation technique uses an array of encoded strings that are reordered by an initialization function, plus a decoder function that retrieves the correct strings based on hex indices. This makes the code harder to read but doesn't change its fundamental purpose.

The decoded function essentially works as:
```javascript
function findFirstDuplicate(arr) {
    const seen = new Set();
    for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (seen.has(arr[i])) return arr[i];
        else seen.add(arr[i]);
    }
    return -1;
}
```

